# graphify: files to keep OUT of the knowledge graph.
#
# gitignore syntax. Per graphify's loader this can only ever exclude MORE than
# .gitignore — a pattern here can never re-include something git ignores.
#
# Why this file exists: `tests/fixtures/diagrams/render/mermaid.min.js` is a
# vendored, minified bundle kept deliberately as a render fixture, so it is
# git-tracked and .gitignore cannot exclude it. AST extraction walks every
# minified symbol in it and emits 2,167 nodes — 35% of the entire graph from a
# single file, all of it noise that crowds out real code in god-node and
# community analysis.
#
# It was filtered out by hand on 2026-08-10, then silently returned: the
# globally-seeded .git/hooks/post-commit runs `graphify update` after every
# commit, which re-extracts from a clean detect and knows nothing about a
# one-off manual filter. Only an ignore file makes the exclusion durable.

# Minified/vendored bundles — no readable symbols, enormous node counts.
*.min.js
*.min.css
